#
# Conformance case: transaction/concurrent-serializable.
#
# A logic:ConcurrentComposition runs two legs that both write the SAME situation.
# The engine EXECUTES both legs over the shared start, DERIVES the
# logic:ConcurrentHistory from their step footprints under the deterministic
# index-order interleaving, and classifies it: the single read/write conflict
# yields ONE logic:precedes edge (left precedes right) — an acyclic history that
# reduces to a serial order, so NO logic:SerializationAnomaly is raised. This is
# the serializable half of the conflict-serializability contract.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live
# in input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/concurrent-serializable/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the Evolution facet that classifies this
# transaction program. logic:TransactionPathEvolution drives certification to the
# transaction-path decidability class (conflict-serializability; PTIME classification,
# not search).
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution .
